# Cloudflare reads this file at deploy (Workers static assets). Rules are
# matched by path; a request gets the headers of every rule it matches.

# Security headers for every response. The site takes no input and loads no
# third-party scripts, so these cost nothing and close off framing, MIME
# sniffing and referrer leaks.
# - HSTS starts at 5 minutes. Once the site is confirmed fine over HTTPS only,
#   raise it to `max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains`.
# - The CSP covers framing and plugins only. A script-src policy is left out on
#   purpose: the static export inlines scripts (React Server Components
#   payloads, the next-themes script), so it would need trialling with
#   Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only first.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=300
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), microphone=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups

# Next.js puts a content hash in every file name under /_next/static/, so a
# changed file always gets a new URL and these can be cached for a year.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Next.js writes the generated share images without a file extension, so tell
# Cloudflare their content type explicitly.
/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
/twitter-image
  Content-Type: image/png
